          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now answer the following questions:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.114,
            0.792,
            0.135
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) Find the average number of points scored per game by A."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.139,
            0.847,
            0.18
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) To find the mean number of points scored per game by C, would you divide the total points by 3 or by 4? Why? What about B?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.185,
            0.505,
            0.205
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(c) Who is the best performer?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.216,
            0.848,
            0.314
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. The marks (out of 100) obtained by a group of students in a General Knowledge quiz are 85, 76, 90, 85, 39, 48, 56, 95, 81 and 75. Another group’s scores in the same quiz are 68, 59, 73, 86, 47, 79, 90, 93 and 86. Compare and describe both the groups performance using, mean and median."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.193,
            0.346,
            0.841,
            0.445
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_caption",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.151,
                0.32,
                0.714,
                0.341
              ],
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "content": "4. Consider this data collected from a survey of a colony."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 7,
              "bbox": [
                0.193,
                0.346,
                0.841,
                0.445
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_33_table_7.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Favourite Sport</td><td>Cricket</td><td>Basket Ball</td><td>Swimming</td><td>Hockey</td><td>Athletics</td></tr><tr><td>Watching</td><td>1240</td><td>470</td><td>510</td><td>430</td><td>250</td></tr><tr><td>Participating</td><td>620</td><td>320</td><td>320</td><td>250</td><td>105</td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.458,
            0.846,
            0.498
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Choose an appropriate scale and draw a double-bar graph. Write down your observations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.502,
            0.849,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "5. Consider a group of 17 students with the following heights (in cm): 106, 110, 123, 125, 117, 120, 112, 115, 110, 120, 115, 102, 115, 115, 109, 115, 101. The sports teacher wants to divide the class into two groups so that each group has an equal number of students: one group has students with height less than a particular height and the other group has students with heights greater than the particular height. Suggest a way to do this. Can you guess the age of these students based on the tabular data in the ‘Telling Tall Tales’ section?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.686,
            0.847,
            0.726
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "6. Describe the mean and median of heights of your class. You can visualise the heights on a dot plot."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.731,
            0.849,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. There are two 7th grade sections at a school. Each section has 15 boys and 15 girls. In one section, the mean height of students is 154.2 cm. From this information, what must be true about the mean height of students in the other section?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.187,
            0.816,
            0.821,
            0.837
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(a) The mean height of students in the other section is 154.2 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.188,
            0.841,
            0.847,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(b) The mean height of students in the other section is less than 154.2 cm."
            }
          ]
        },
